.TH NYSM-DESKTOP 1 "" "Now You See Me" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nysm-desktop \- desktop app of Now You See Me
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nysm-desktop
[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-theme\fR \fIsystem\fR|\fIlight\fR|\fIdark\fR]
[\fB\-\-attach\fR \fIauto\fR|\fInever\fR|\fIrequire\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nysm-desktop
is a GTK 4 window with pages for the system overview, CPU, memory,
network, storage, containers and services, processes (filter, sort, group
by app, select and watch, live details) and an About page that shows what
the app itself costs right now. Charts cover recent history kept in memory
by the shared collector
.RB ( "nysm service run" ),
or by the window itself when no collector runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " name"
Open on overview, cpu, memory, network, storage, groups, processes or
about.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fIsystem\fR|\fIlight\fR|\fIdark\fR
Colour scheme; the default follows the desktop.
.TP
.BR \-\-attach " " \fIauto\fR|\fInever\fR|\fIrequire\fR
Use the shared collector when available (default), never, or only.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
All options, including screenshot aids.
.SH KEYS
Alt+1 to Alt+7 switch pages, Ctrl+F filters processes, Ctrl+comma opens
settings, Ctrl+W or Ctrl+Q closes the window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nysm/config.toml
Settings (history length, theme, container names, top bar).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nysm (1),
.BR nysm-tray (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sheheemmulakkal/now-you-see-me
